# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_empty_files_clear.py" "EMPTY FILES CLEAR GATE: PASS" "empty-files wrong-clear (an empty changed-files API response no longer silently clears a PR)" "empty-files wrong-clear silent-miss (a wrong-clear-on-error): GitHub's changed-files API can return an EMPTY list on a 200 WITHOUT raising (a proxy/CDN edge serving an empty body, a 204, eventual-consistency right after a push). That empty list bypasses the fetch try/except in webhook_handlers (which only catches a RAISE) and is then INDISTINGUISHABLE from a genuine 0-file PR, so the brain runs reconcile(cid, ..., []) [RELEASING the PR's lanes] and renders 'success' [clear to land] -- a SILENT MISS over a real overlap. WORSE on a synchronize: a PR that was correctly action_required flips to success AND drops out of the in-flight set [its real collision counterpart loses its partner]; if that is the last event before merge, it merges GREEN over a real collision. THE FIX [recall-safe]: cross-check the empty file list against the PR's OWN changed-files COUNT -- the pull_request object carries changed_files [an int] independently of the Files API [in the webhook payload AND get_pull_request / GET /pulls/{n}]. A RAW [pre-_code_paths] empty list while the PR object reports changed_files > 0 is a PROVABLE read failure -> HONEST-UNKNOWN: do NOT analyze [so reconcile never releases this PR's lanes -- the real collision stays surfaced on the counterpart] and post an advisory 'neutral' 'couldn't read changed files -- not analyzed' [NEVER success]. The genuine 0-code-file case is PRESERVED: a docs-only PR returns a NON-empty raw list [README.md etc.] that _code_paths filters to [] -> raw is non-empty -> the guard does not fire -> it stays 'success'. A real 0-FILE PR reports changed_files==0 -> the guard does not fire either [recall-safe]. Content-free, never-crash [the count is read defensively; a non-int/missing field reads as 0 = guard off]. Drives the REAL handler [server.handle_event] over the REAL gate [db/schema.sql] with a FakeGitHub whose Files API returns [] for the chosen PRs" "empty-files wrong-clear: an empty changed-files API response on a 200 [non-raising] no longer silently clears a PR or releases its lanes -- cross-checked against the PR's own changed_files count it becomes an advisory 'not analyzed' [neutral], the real collision stays on the counterpart, and the genuine docs-only / 0-file cases stay 'success' [recall-safe]" 20
